---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="Refund policy for Hekara sponsorship and paid services."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted mb-4">Last updated: November 2024</p>

      <h2>1. Sponsorship</h2>

      <p>
        <strong>Sponsorship is non-refundable.</strong> Once your payment is processed through GitHub Sponsors or similar platform, it cannot be refunded.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Sponsorship is a voluntary gift to support the project</li>
        <li>It is not a purchase of a product or service</li>
        <li>No refunds will be issued except as required by law (chargebacks, payment disputes)</li>
        <li>Canceling your sponsorship stops future recurring payments but does not refund past payments</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Free Software</h2>

      <p>
        Hekara is provided free under AGPL-3.0 license. There are no refunds because there is no payment.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Paid Services (Custom Solutions)</h2>

      <p>
        If you have engaged us for custom development, integrations, or consulting work under a Statement of Work (SOW):
      </p>

      <h3>Refund eligibility</h3>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Before work starts:</strong> Cancel within 48 hours of signing for a full refund</li>
        <li><strong>After work starts:</strong> No refunds. You pay for work completed per the SOW milestones</li>
        <li><strong>Partial completion:</strong> Pay for completed deliverables only. If you cancel mid-project, you owe payment for all work up to cancellation plus any out-of-pocket expenses incurred</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Dispute resolution</h3>

      <p>
        If you believe work does not meet the SOW requirements:
      </p>

      <ol>
        <li>Notify us in writing within 14 days of delivery</li>
        <li>Describe the specific unmet requirement and evidence</li>
        <li>We will investigate and either fix it (if it's a defect) or explain why it meets the SOW</li>
        <li>If unresolved after good-faith discussion, either party may escalate per the SOW dispute clause</li>
      </ol>

      <p>
        <strong>Refunds for defects:</strong> If work has a material defect and cannot be fixed, we will refund the payment for that deliverable only, not cancellation of the entire SOW.
      </p>

      <h3>What is NOT refundable</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>Time spent (whether work was useful to you or not)</li>
        <li>Out-of-pocket costs incurred (travel, software licenses, infrastructure)</li>
        <li>Opportunity cost or lost business value</li>
        <li>Decisions you made based on our work (even if the advice changed or became outdated)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Payment Disputes</h2>

      <p>
        <strong>Chargebacks:</strong> If you initiate a chargeback on a legitimate payment for delivered work, we reserve the right to:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Report it to payment processors</li>
        <li>Refuse future work with you</li>
        <li>Take legal action to recover the disputed amount plus processing fees</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        If you have a legitimate concern, contact us directly before initiating a chargeback.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Paid Support & SLAs</h2>

      <p>
        If you purchase a support package with SLAs:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>SLA compliance:</strong> We guarantee response times and availability per the signed agreement</li>
        <li><strong>SLA breach:</strong> If we breach SLA, you receive service credits toward future support, not a refund of past payments</li>
        <li><strong>Excessive claims:</strong> If you file more than 3 false SLA breach claims per quarter, your support package may be terminated for cause</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Platform Refunds (GitHub, Stripe, etc.)</h2>

      <p>
        <strong>Payments through third parties:</strong> GitHub Sponsors, Stripe, and PayPal have their own refund policies. Those policies may allow refunds even if ours do not.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>If your payment platform refunds you, we accept that as final</li>
        <li>We will not dispute platform refunds</li>
        <li>If your platform refunds a sponsorship, we consider that a cancellation</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Tax & Legal</h2>

      <p>
        <strong>Taxes:</strong> You are responsible for any taxes owed on sponsorship or consulting payments. The maintainer is not responsible for tax reporting on your behalf.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Governing law:</strong> These terms are governed by the laws of India. Disputes may be resolved by arbitration or court proceedings per the dispute resolution clause in your SOW.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>

      <p>
        For refund requests or payment disputes, <a href="/Hekara/contact">contact us</a> with:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Your payment reference number</li>
        <li>Transaction date and amount</li>
        <li>Reason for refund request</li>
        <li>Any supporting documentation (SOW, emails, deliverables)</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        We will respond within 5 business days.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
